*.parquet
*.pkl
dropshotdata/raw/
dropshotdata/manifest/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# trained models and raw downloaded data stay out of git (piggyback/GitHub
# Releases instead) - *.parquet/*.pkl above already cover most of this, but
# xgb model caches save as .json and the tennismylife bridge pulls raw CSVs
# directly into tune_scratch
dropshotdata/tune_scratch/xgb_bagged_model_cache*/
dropshotdata/tune_scratch/tml_2026_*.csv
dropshotdata/tune_scratch/us_open_2026_predictions.json
# elo_compact.py's derived array cache (4.8 MB .npz - not covered by the
# *.parquet/*.pkl rules above). Rebuilt from the archive in ~2 minutes by
# `python dropshotdata/tune_scratch/elo_compact.py --force`, so it is a cache,
# not data worth versioning.
dropshotdata/tune_scratch/elo_compact_cache.npz
# stdout/stderr from detached screen runs - regenerated every run, and the
# results themselves land in the per-arm parquet checkpoints
dropshotdata/tune_scratch/*.log
dropshotdata/tune_scratch/*.err
# release build staging - assets are published to GitHub Releases, never committed
# (a 137 MB tarball got swept in here once by `git add -A` and silently stalled
# every push; GitHub also hard-rejects blobs over 100 MB)
dropshotdata/tune_scratch/_release_stage/

# generated site payloads - regenerated by the pipeline, published to R2, not git
dropshotdata/blog/us_open_2026_live_predictions.json
dropshotdata/blog/us_open_2026_drawonly.json

# wrangler's local cache/temp dir (created wherever it's invoked from)
.wrangler/
